    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "📋 Incident Escalation Policy & Alert Conditions",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### 🛡️ Enterprise SLA & Alert Evaluation Rules\n\n| Alert Trigger Condition | Severity | SLA Window | Automated Action Taken |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **`router_up == 0`** or **`router_ping_latency_ms == 0`** | **🚨 P1 CRITICAL** | **5 Seconds** | Dispatches immediate Telegram P1 Outage alert, creates **ServiceNow Incident (#INC)**, initiates NOC escalation ladder (5s, 2m, 10m, 12h, 24h, 1w, 1mo). |\n| **`router_up == 1`** and **`router_ping_latency_ms > 0`** | **✅ RESOLVED** | **Immediate (< 2s)** | Auto-resolves ServiceNow Incident with **`Actual End`** timestamp, sends Telegram recovery alert, dispatches **`BOOT LINK STABILIZED`** notice. |\n| **`router_ping_latency_ms > 50 ms`** | **⚠️ WARNING** | **Sustained 60s** | Flags Wi-Fi congestion / high RF interference on Grafana dashboard. |\n\n> **Note on Zero Latency:** An ICMP Ping Latency of **0 ms** represents complete packet loss / host unreachable (power-off or disconnected cable). A healthy local link operates between **0.5 ms and 5.0 ms**."
      }
    }
